the ability to ripple water with the  power of your voice is the worst  superhero power ever so how is Tony  creating these watery ripples it's not  Tony's voice that's causing the ripples  it's hundreds of baby mosquitoes these  mosquitoes are in their larval stage so  they're living just under the surface of  the water and when he shouts they think  it's a predator and they dive it's rare  to see this because the timing has to be  just right  mosquitoes were only in the larval stage  for about seven to ten days while  they're living just under the surface of  the water eating plankton  the reason the mosquito larvae can exist  under the surface of the water and not  drown is because they have little tiny  siphons like a snorkel that sits out  above the water  Tony's screaming is so loud that he  actually creates pressure waves that  disturb the surface of the water the  ultra sensitive siphons of the mosquito  larvae can detect this disturbance and  that's what causes them to instinctively  dive down and try to get away now that  he's seen it once I love the idea that  Tony is roaming around the world just  shouting at random lakes hoping that  it'll happen again next time  [Music]
 

